  "officialHtml": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/pdab100-300.html",
  "prefLabel": "Pdab 202.10 Record",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Pdab 202.10 Record.\n\n(a) The record in a proceeding shall include all of the following that are applicable in that case:\n\n(1) All pleadings, motions, objections, and rulings;\n\n(2) Evidence received or considered;\n\n(3) A statement of matters officially noticed;\n\n(4) Any decision, opinion, or report by the board;\n\n(5) The recording or stenographic notes or symbols prepared for the proceeding by the board, together with any transcript of all or part of the hearing considered before final disposition of the adjudicative proceeding;\n\n(6) Staff memoranda or data submitted to the board; and\n\n(7) Matters placed on the record after an ex parte communication.\n\n(b) The record in part or in its entirety shall be exempt from public disclosure if it is identified as confidential information as defined in Pdab 201.02(d) in accordance with RSA 91-A:5.\n\nSource. #13500-A, eff 12-2-22",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/pdab100-300.html"
